; A hand-written zone whose only job is to contain what a machine-generated one
; cannot. The DNSSEC fixtures are named-compilezone output: one record per line,
; every name written out in full, every TTL a bare number. Three findings in a
; row hid behind that shape rather than behind the code — a relative wildcard
; (51) and a bracketed ::1 (50) could not appear in the corpus at all, and so
; could not be refuted by it.
;
; Nothing serves this file. fixtures/bind/interop.test.zone is the one four
; foreign servers are handed, and it has to stay as it is: two interop tests ask
; it for nothing-here.interop.test and require NXDOMAIN, which a wildcard would
; quietly answer instead.
;
; named-checkzone is the judge. Its flattened output is what Hermod's reading is
; compared against, record for record.

$ORIGIN format.test.
$TTL 1h

@           IN  SOA ns1 hostmaster (
                    2026091501  ; serial
                    2h          ; refresh, in units
                    900         ; retry, bare
                    1209600     ; expire
                    1h )        ; minimum

@           IN  NS    ns1

; Relative names, including the one that reaches the origin through @ above.
ns1         IN  A     192.0.2.53
a           IN  A     192.0.2.1

; A bare wildcard: the way every hand-written zone spells one, and the exact
; shape of finding 51.
*           IN  A     192.0.2.98

; And a wildcard one label down, which parses differently because the fragment
; is a valid name on its own.
*.sub       IN  A     192.0.2.97

; The two addresses whose text form IPv6Address.ToString() bracketed — finding
; 50 — plus the fully expanded form that has to come back canonical.
loopback    IN  AAAA  ::1
unspec      IN  AAAA  ::
expanded    IN  AAAA  2001:0db8:0000:0000:0000:0000:0000:0001
single      IN  AAAA  2001:db8:0:1:1:1:1:1

; TTLs written with BIND's units rather than as a count of seconds.
hour        1h  IN  A 192.0.2.61
day         2d  IN  A 192.0.2.62
week        1w  IN  A 192.0.2.63
mixed       90m IN  A 192.0.2.64

; A name whose case is not the zone's, which RFC 4343 makes the same name.
MiXeDcAsE   IN  A     192.0.2.65

; Underscore names (RFC 8552), which hostname syntax refuses.
_svc._tcp   IN  TXT   "an underscore name"
_dmarc      IN  TXT   "v=DMARC1; p=none"

; A type with no mnemonic, in the RFC 3597 §5 generic form.
generic     IN  TYPE65280 \# 4 deadbeef

; An absolute name in a file that is otherwise relative.
outside     IN  CNAME a.format.test.

; Parenthesised continuation outside the SOA, and a comment inside it.
multiline   IN  TXT   ( "first"      ; a comment mid-record
                        "second" )
